        "id": "b1",
        "chapter_id": "ch1",
        "text": "Two strangers named Eli Vale stood together at the harbor counter. One Eli Vale was a harbor pilot. The other Eli Vale was a clockmaker. They were different people, born in different towns, and they had never met before that morning.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch1.xhtml",
          "element_id": "b1",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b2",
        "chapter_id": "ch1",
        "text": "Eli Vale the pilot signed the shipping register with his left hand. Beside him, Eli Vale the clockmaker signed a separate repair receipt with his right hand. Each man held his own distinct document.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch1.xhtml",
          "element_id": "b2",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b3",
        "chapter_id": "ch2",
        "text": "The harbor pilot Eli Vale took his boat out while the clockmaker Eli Vale stayed at the counter to mend a wall clock. The pilot could not have been the clockmaker: both men had stood face to face at the same time.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch2.xhtml",
